# Blog Post Generation Rules

When asked to generate a blog post, follow these rules:

## Inputs Required
- 1-3 target keywords (e.g., "small business SEO India", "why my website has no traffic")
- Optional: specific angle or audience

## Output Format
Create a markdown file at `src/content/blog/{slug}.md` with:

```markdown
---
title: "Engaging title that includes the primary keyword naturally"
description: "2-sentence meta description under 160 characters, includes keyword"
date: YYYY-MM-DD (use today's date)
tags: ["Category"]  (pick from: Website, Google, SEO, Ads, Marketing, Social Media, Email, Business)
keywords: ["keyword 1", "keyword 2", "keyword 3"]
---
```

## Writing Style (CRITICAL)

1. **Audience**: Indian small business owners (shopkeepers, manufacturers, traders, service providers)
2. **Tone**: Direct, slightly provocative, conversational. Like explaining to a smart friend who isn't tech-savvy.
3. **NO jargon**: Never use terms like "ROI", "conversion rate", "CTR", "funnel", "engagement metrics" without immediately explaining them in plain language
4. **Use Indian context**: Mention rupees (₹), Indian cities, Indian business types (kirana, manufacturing, trading), Indian platforms (JustDial, IndiaMART)
5. **Length**: 800-1200 words (enough for SEO, not so long people bounce)
6. **Structure**: 
   - Hook (1 paragraph that states the problem bluntly)
   - 3-5 sections with H2 headings
   - Each section: problem → why it happens → what to do
   - End with a CTA linking to [KhojKaro.in](https://khojkaro.in)

## SEO Requirements

- Primary keyword in title, first paragraph, and at least one H2
- Natural keyword density (don't stuff)
- Internal links to other blog posts when relevant
- External link to khojkaro.in in the closing CTA
- Meta description under 160 chars that makes people want to click

## CTA Template (use at the end of every post)

```markdown
---

*[Contextual sentence about needing help]? Our team at [KhojKaro.in](https://khojkaro.in) [what they do for this specific topic] — plain language, no tech jargon.*
```

## File Naming
- Use lowercase, hyphen-separated slug derived from title
- Example: `why-your-website-isnt-getting-customers.md`

## Tags Reference
| Tag | Use for |
|-----|---------|
| Website | Website issues, design, mobile, speed |
| Google | Google Business Profile, search ranking, Maps |
| SEO | Search optimization, keywords, backlinks |
| Ads | Google Ads, Facebook Ads, Instagram Ads, budgets |
| Marketing | General marketing strategy, offline-to-online |
| Social Media | Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube |
| Email | Email marketing, newsletters |
| Business | General business advice, compliance, loans |
